     *
     * **`variants_status` — read it before you render a variant URL.** Every
     * `variant_<size>_url` in this response is derived from `<type>/<hash>`, so
     * all of them are present and well-formed in the 201 that creates the row,
     * *before* the background task has written a single file. `variants_status`
     * is `"pending"` until generation succeeds and `"ready"` afterwards
     * (`variants_ready_at` carries the moment, null while pending). A `pending`
     * payload's variant URLs are a prediction, not a resource; poll the media ref
     * (`/file-exists/`) or fall back to `original_url` until it reads `ready`.
     * A row that stays `pending` is a broken pipeline, not a slow one — see
     * `checks.W008`.
     *
     * **Request format:** `multipart/form-data` with `file` field
     *
     * **Maximum file size:** `STAPEL_CDN\["MAX_IMAGE_SIZE"\]`, 20MB by default.
     * Enforced before the body is hashed; over it the answer is 413.
     *
     * **Stored type:** the `type` form field, validated against
     * `STAPEL_CDN\["ASSET_TYPES"\]` (400 `error.400.invalid_image_type` otherwise).
     * Without it: `STAPEL_CDN\["DEFAULT_UPLOAD_TYPE"\]` when a deployment names one,
     * else the sole `ASSET_TYPES` entry. A deployment with several asset types and
     * no `DEFAULT_UPLOAD_TYPE` has no default: the request answers
     * 400 `error.400.image_type_required`. A `DEFAULT_UPLOAD_TYPE` naming a value
     * absent from `ASSET_TYPES` is a misconfiguration: this endpoint answers 400 and
     * `stapel_cdn.assets.W014` reports it at boot.
     *
     * Wire: `POST /cdn/api/v1/upload/image/`   `upload_image`
     *
     * Permissions: IsNotAnonymousUser
     *
     * Auth: required
     *
     * Errors (bound by contract):
     * - `FileTypeNotAllowed` (400) — File type not allowed
     * - `ImageTypeRequired` (400) — Image type is required
     * - `InvalidFormat` (400) — Unsupported file format
     * - `InvalidImageType` (400) — Invalid image type
     * - `StorageQuotaExceeded` (403) — Storage quota exceeded
     * - `FileTooLarge` (413) — File is too large
     * - `Internal` (500) — Something went wrong
     * - `ImageDecoderUnavailable` (503) — This server cannot process {extension} images right now
     * - statuses 401 (codes not bound in the contract)
     *
     * Example response (Image uploaded):
     * ```json
     * {
     *     "image": {
     *         "created_at": "2026-03-17T10:30:00Z",
     *         "file_extension": ".jpg",
     *         "file_hash": "9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
     *         "id": 42,
     *         "is_processed": false,
     *         "original_filename": "photo.jpg",
     *         "original_height": 1080,
     *         "original_size": 2048576,
     *         "original_url": "/media/cdn/images/original/9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08.jpg",
     *         "original_width": 1920,
     *         "prefix": "avatar/9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
     *         "render_meta": {
     *             "animated": false,
     *             "aspect": 1.7778,
     *             "bytes": 2048576,
     *             "ext": ".jpg",
     *             "height": 1080,
     *             "kind": "image",
     * …
     * ```
     *
     * @return `ImageUploadResponse` (200, 201)
     *
     * @param file The file to upload. Images: jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp, avif, heic, heif. Videos: mp4, webm, mov, avi, mkv.
     * @param type Asset type, one of STAPEL_CDN\['ASSET_TYPES'\]. Required when the deployment has several types and no DEFAULT_UPLOAD_TYPE.
     * @param onProgress Upload progress `(sent, total)` in bytes.
     */
    public suspend fun uploadImage(
        `file`: FilePart,
        type: String? = null,
        onProgress: ((sent: Long, total: Long?) -> Unit)? = null,
    ): StapelResult<ImageUploadResponse, UploadImageError>

    /**
     * Upload an image with specific type
     *
     * Upload an image file with a caller-chosen type.
     *
     * **Supported formats:** JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, BMP, HEIC, HEIF
     *
     * **Available types:** every entry of `STAPEL_CDN\["ASSET_TYPES"\]` — the same
     * setting `TypeEnum` in this document is generated from. The zero-infra
     * default is `("avatar",)`; anything else answers
     * `error.400.invalid_image_type`.
     *
     * **Maximum file size:** `STAPEL_CDN\["MAX_IMAGE_SIZE"\]`, 20MB by default.
     * Enforced before the body is hashed; over it the answer is 413.
     *
     * Wire: `POST /cdn/api/v1/images/{image_type}/upload/`   `upload_typed_image`
     *
     * Permissions: IsNotAnonymousUser
     *
     * Auth: required
     *
     * Errors (bound by contract):
     * - `FileTypeNotAllowed` (400) — File type not allowed
     * - `InvalidFormat` (400) — Unsupported file format
     * - `InvalidImageType` (400) — Invalid image type
     * - `StorageQuotaExceeded` (403) — Storage quota exceeded
     * - `FileTooLarge` (413) — File is too large
     * - `Internal` (500) — Something went wrong
     * - `ImageDecoderUnavailable` (503) — This server cannot process {extension} images right now
     * - statuses 401 (codes not bound in the contract)
     *
     * Example response (Image uploaded):
     * ```json
     * {
     *     "image": {
     *         "created_at": "2026-03-17T10:30:00Z",
     *         "file_extension": ".jpg",
     *         "file_hash": "9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
     *         "id": 42,
     *         "is_processed": false,
     *         "original_filename": "photo.jpg",
     *         "original_height": 1080,
     *         "original_size": 2048576,
     *         "original_url": "/media/cdn/images/original/9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08.jpg",
     *         "original_width": 1920,
     *         "prefix": "avatar/9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
     *         "render_meta": {
     *             "animated": false,
     *             "aspect": 1.7778,
     *             "bytes": 2048576,
     *             "ext": ".jpg",
     *             "height": 1080,
     *             "kind": "image",
     * …
     * ```
     *
     * @return `ImageUploadResponse` (200, 201)
     * @param file Image file to upload
     * @param onProgress Upload progress `(sent, total)` in bytes.
     */
    public suspend fun uploadTypedImage(
        imageType: String,
        `file`: FilePart,
        onProgress: ((sent: Long, total: Long?) -> Unit)? = null,
    ): StapelResult<ImageUploadResponse, UploadTypedImageError>

    /**
     * Upload a video
     *
     * Upload a video file for processing.
     *
     * **Supported formats:** MP4, WebM, MOV, AVI, MKV
     *
     * **What happens on upload:**
     * 1. File hash (SHA-256) is calculated for deduplication
     * 2. If file already exists, returns existing video data (200 OK)
     * 3. If new file, creates video record
     * 4. Variant generation via FFmpeg (TODO: not yet implemented)
     *
     * **Planned variants:**
     * - 16p, 32p - animated thumbnails
     * - 240p, 480p, 720p, 1080p, 2160p - video resolutions
     *
     * **Request format:** `multipart/form-data` with `file` field
     *
     * **Maximum file size:** `STAPEL_CDN\["MAX_VIDEO_SIZE"\]`, 100MB by default.
     * Enforced before the body is hashed; over it the answer is 413.
     *
     * Wire: `POST /cdn/api/v1/upload/video/`   `upload_video`
     *
     * Permissions: IsNotAnonymousUser
     *
     * Auth: required
     *
     * Errors (bound by contract):
     * - `FileTypeNotAllowed` (400) — File type not allowed
     * - `InvalidFormat` (400) — Unsupported file format
     * - `StorageQuotaExceeded` (403) — Storage quota exceeded
     * - `FileTooLarge` (413) — File is too large
     * - `Internal` (500) — Something went wrong
     * - statuses 401 (codes not bound in the contract)
     *
     * Example response (Video uploaded):
     * ```json
     * {
     *     "message": "Video uploaded successfully (variant generation not yet implemented)",
     *     "video": {
     *         "created_at": "2026-03-17T10:30:00Z",
     *         "duration": 12.5,
     *         "file_extension": ".mp4",
     *         "file_hash": "9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
     *         "id": 7,
     *         "is_processed": false,
     *         "original_filename": "clip.mp4",
     *         "original_height": 1080,
     *         "original_size": 15728640,
     *         "original_url": "/media/cdn/videos/original/9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08.mp4",
     *         "original_width": 1920,
     *         "poster_url": null,
     *         "render_meta": {
     *             "aspect": 1.7778,
     *             "bytes": 15728640,
     *             "duration_ms": 12500,
     *             "ext": ".mp4",
     * …
     * ```
     *
     * @return `VideoUploadResponse` (200, 201)
     *
     * @param file Video file to upload (mp4, webm, mov, avi, mkv)
     * @param onProgress Upload progress `(sent, total)` in bytes.
     */
    public suspend fun uploadVideo(`file`: FilePart, onProgress: ((sent: Long, total: Long?) -> Unit)? = null): StapelResult<VideoUploadResponse, UploadVideoError>
}
